<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  How the powers feel about a colony, based on what that colony believes.

  This is the version of "the Society hates the resistance" that RimWorld can
  actually express. Decompiling GoodwillSituationWorker showed every method takes
  only `Faction other`, and the concrete workers resolve the second party as
  Faction.OfPlayer - so a mod cannot set how two NPC factions feel about each
  other. What it CAN set is how a faction feels about the player, which is the
  only relationship the game simulates with any weight anyway.

  Structure mirrored from Ideology/Defs/Goodwill/GoodwillSituations_MemeCompatibility.xml,
  which uses GoodwillSituationWorker_MemeCompatibility with <meme> and <otherMeme>.
  The worker checks the pairing in both directions, so one def covers both
  "we believe X and they believe Y" and the reverse.

  The Society and the Rim Dominion both require RR_ColorHierarchy; the Sons of
  Ares require RR_ColorEquality. So a colony that adopts the hierarchy is embraced
  by the Society and loathed by the resistance, and a colony that rejects it gets
  the reverse - without a line of C#.

  Magnitudes are set against vanilla's meme-compatibility range, which runs
  roughly +10 for agreement and -10 to -20 for the sharper disagreements. These
  sit at the harsh end because the hierarchy is the entire quarrel.
-->
<Defs>

  <!-- ============================== agreement ============================= -->

  <GoodwillSituationDef>
    <defName>RR_ColorHierarchy_Agreement</defName>
    <label>Color hierarchy agreement</label>
    <workerClass>GoodwillSituationWorker_MemeCompatibility</workerClass>
    <meme>RR_ColorHierarchy</meme>
    <otherMeme>RR_ColorHierarchy</otherMeme>
    <naturalGoodwillOffset>20</naturalGoodwillOffset>
  </GoodwillSituationDef>

  <GoodwillSituationDef>
    <defName>RR_ColorEquality_Agreement</defName>
    <label>Color equality agreement</label>
    <workerClass>GoodwillSituationWorker_MemeCompatibility</workerClass>
    <meme>RR_ColorEquality</meme>
    <otherMeme>RR_ColorEquality</otherMeme>
    <naturalGoodwillOffset>20</naturalGoodwillOffset>
  </GoodwillSituationDef>

  <!-- ============================ disagreement ============================ -->

  <GoodwillSituationDef>
    <defName>RR_ColorOrder_Disagreement</defName>
    <label>Color hierarchy disagreement</label>
    <workerClass>GoodwillSituationWorker_MemeCompatibility</workerClass>
    <meme>RR_ColorHierarchy</meme>
    <otherMeme>RR_ColorEquality</otherMeme>
    <naturalGoodwillOffset>-40</naturalGoodwillOffset>
  </GoodwillSituationDef>

  <!--
    Rejecting the hierarchy while the other party holds it is not a disagreement
    about policy, it is a denial that they are people. Slavery disapproval is the
    nearest vanilla analogue and it runs to -20; this runs further.
  -->
  <GoodwillSituationDef>
    <defName>RR_ColorHierarchy_VersusEgalitarian</defName>
    <label>rejects the Colors</label>
    <workerClass>GoodwillSituationWorker_MemeCompatibility</workerClass>
    <meme>RR_ColorEquality</meme>
    <otherMeme>RR_ColorHierarchy</otherMeme>
    <naturalGoodwillOffset>-40</naturalGoodwillOffset>
  </GoodwillSituationDef>

  <!-- ========================= the tribes' position ======================= -->

  <!--
    Gold worship and the Society's doctrine are not the same belief, but they
    point the same way, and the Society engineered the tribes' religion precisely
    so they would. Warm rather than identical.
  -->
  <GoodwillSituationDef>
    <defName>RR_GoldWorship_WithHierarchy</defName>
    <label>reveres the sky gods</label>
    <workerClass>GoodwillSituationWorker_MemeCompatibility</workerClass>
    <meme>RR_GoldWorship</meme>
    <otherMeme>RR_ColorHierarchy</otherMeme>
    <naturalGoodwillOffset>15</naturalGoodwillOffset>
  </GoodwillSituationDef>

  <GoodwillSituationDef>
    <defName>RR_GoldWorship_Agreement</defName>
    <label>sky god agreement</label>
    <workerClass>GoodwillSituationWorker_MemeCompatibility</workerClass>
    <meme>RR_GoldWorship</meme>
    <otherMeme>RR_GoldWorship</otherMeme>
    <naturalGoodwillOffset>20</naturalGoodwillOffset>
  </GoodwillSituationDef>

  <!--
    A colony saying the gods are neither gods nor owed anything is not a rival
    faith to the tribes, it is blasphemy - and one the shamans were paid to make
    unthinkable.
  -->
  <GoodwillSituationDef>
    <defName>RR_GoldWorship_VersusEgalitarian</defName>
    <label>denies the sky gods</label>
    <workerClass>GoodwillSituationWorker_MemeCompatibility</workerClass>
    <meme>RR_GoldWorship</meme>
    <otherMeme>RR_ColorEquality</otherMeme>
    <naturalGoodwillOffset>-35</naturalGoodwillOffset>
  </GoodwillSituationDef>

</Defs>
